content.thinking:
The user wants to prefill the address field when editing a user. Looking at the code, there's already a useEffect that tries to prefill the address from the user object:

```javascript
useEffect(() => {
  if (user?.address) {
    setFormData((prev: any) => ({
      ...prev,
      address: user.address,
    }));
  }
}, [user]);
```

However, the issue is that the Google PlaceAutocompleteElement is a custom web component that doesn't use a standard input element. So even if `formData.address` is set, the PlaceAutocompleteElement won't display that value automatically.

To fix this, I need to set the value of the PlaceAutocompleteElement after it's created. The PlaceAutocompleteElement has a `value` property that can be set programmatically.

Let me update the useEffect that creates the PlaceAutocompleteElement to set its value from formData.address if it exists.

